WEBVTT

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:03.920
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:09.870
Did you do this?

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:11.960
Huh?  Of course not.

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:18.370
Are you Revolver?

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:21.380
Hey, Playmaker!

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:24.780
Someone's dueling over there.

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:29.740
He's full of vigor!

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:31.620
Revolver...

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:36.350
Topologic Bomber Dragon's effect activates!

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:38.450
Full Overlap!

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:43.670
Now Go Onizuka has two Link Monsters.

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:46.880
And he's still allowed to Normal Summon.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:49.130
And he has six cards in his hand!

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:51.860
But why is he confident?

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:56.470
All right!  Now he has four Link Monsters!

00:00:56.470 --> 00:01:01.830
Battle!  Great Ogre attacks you directly!

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:06.420
Sink into the abyss of bottomless despair!

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:11.590
This light is...

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:17.520
I activate the trap card, Mirror Force.

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:21.990
All your monsters in attack 
position are destroyed!

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:32.140
The terrifying card that Playmaker 
mentioned was Mirror Force!

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:37.330
Since Link Monsters can't be placed in 
defense, it's the perfect prey for Mirror Force.

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:43.890
Link Protection's true goal was to 
destroy Go Onizuka's Link Monsters.

00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:45.620
I see!

00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:12.880
I run Across the universe

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:15.930
At the speed of light

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:17.890
Begin Loading

00:02:17.890 --> 00:02:21.530
Open the door of dreams

00:02:22.030 --> 00:02:25.190
VRAINS spreads

00:02:25.190 --> 00:02:28.230
Believe in myself

00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:31.830
VRAINS continues

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:37.150
The circuit draws the future

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:41.120
I'll grab it with my own hands  Yeah

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:42.740
Access!

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:45.530
Start swirling, Data Storm!

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:47.080
I'm now With the Wind

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:49.410
Link with my soul

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:52.220
Speed up, Data Storm!

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:53.920
Now Win the Race

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:56.770
Connected world

00:02:56.770 --> 00:03:00.160
No matter when

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:03.620
Nothing is impossible

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:07.870
Strive for hope

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:12.250
And ride the wind!

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:31.600
They're gone.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.560
They're all destroyed!

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:35.200
Don't worry.

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:38.760
Onizuka will win!  He will!

00:03:41.810 --> 00:03:43.800
Go Onizuka...

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:47.170
Hey!  Hang in there, Go Onizuka!

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:56.580
Hey, did he lose heart?

00:03:56.950 --> 00:03:59.550
If you want to give up, now's the time.

00:04:02.990 --> 00:04:06.210
So you destroyed them all.

00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:08.490
But that erased all my doubts.

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:11.460
I won't back down!

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:19.300
I'll use everything I've built 
up to defeat you, Revolver!

00:04:20.170 --> 00:04:22.770
Gouki Trainer's effect activates!

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:25.580
When there are no monsters on my field...

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:28.740
...I Special Summon it from 
my hand in defense position!

00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:36.070
Trainer's effect lets me Special Summon Great 
Ogre from my graveyard by lowering its ATK by 500!

00:04:36.410 --> 00:04:38.260
I end my turn.

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:40.860
Bring it on, Revolver!

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:46.070
Even if your field is destroyed, you 
resurrect your monsters quickly to face me.

00:04:46.070 --> 00:04:52.040
I'll honor your unbreakable spirit 
by completing crushing you.

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:54.510
My turn!  I draw!

00:04:54.910 --> 00:04:59.240
From my hand, I activate the 
Quick-Play Spell, Quick Launch!

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:03.720
I Special Summon Magnarokket 
Dragon from my deck!

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:12.160
Due to Great Ogre's effect, 
it loses ATK equal to its DEF!

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:14.290
Ogre Pressure!

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:21.500
From my hand, I activate 
the spell card, Squib Draw.

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:29.940
I destroy my Magnarokket to 
draw two cards from my deck!

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:33.910
Then I activate the Field 
Spell, Boot Sector Launch!

00:05:33.910 --> 00:05:38.880
I Special Summon two Rokket monsters 
from my hand in defense position.

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:43.360
I Special Summon Shelrokket and Metalrokket!

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:47.620
Due to Boot Sector Launch's 
additional effect...

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:51.840
...Rokket monsters gain 300 ATK and DEF!

00:05:52.270 --> 00:05:55.820
Appear!  The future circuit 
that lights up my path!

00:05:58.240 --> 00:06:01.110
The summoning conditions are two Rokkets!

00:06:01.110 --> 00:06:06.550
I set Shelrokket and Metalrokket 
in the Link Markers!

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:10.650
Link Summon!

00:06:10.990 --> 00:06:14.820
Appear, Link 2 Booster Dragon!

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:20.980
Then I summon a second 
Shelrokket from my hand.

00:06:23.570 --> 00:06:29.400
Due to the Field Spell Boot Sector 
Launch's effect, it gains 300 ATK.

00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:32.950
Ogre Pressure!

00:06:35.960 --> 00:06:39.860
I activate Booster Dragon's effect!

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:44.180
Shelrokket gains 500 ATK and DEF.

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:50.160
By taking Link Monster's effect, 
Shelrokket's effect activates.

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:51.960
And self-destructs!

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:58.400
Then I destroy a monster that's in the 
same column as this monster's Zone.

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:02.630
And if there's a monster in the 
next Zone, it's also destroyed!

00:07:06.180 --> 00:07:07.440
What?

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:11.410
An effect that activates when 
it's targeted by an effect...

00:07:11.890 --> 00:07:14.380
It's Revolver's specialty.

00:07:14.380 --> 00:07:19.350
This is bad!  Onizuka's monsters 
are really all destroyed!

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:20.820
Battle!

00:07:20.820 --> 00:07:23.790
Booster Dragon attacks you directly!

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:32.300
Onizuka!

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:43.170
I'm still standing!

00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:49.360
Since effects destroyed Magnarokket and 
Shelrokket, their effects activate.

00:07:49.730 --> 00:07:53.340
I Special Summon different 
Rokket monsters from my deck

00:07:53.340 --> 00:07:56.090
in defense position at the end of the turn.

00:07:56.520 --> 00:08:00.340
Appear, Shelrokket and Metalrokket!

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:10.740
Due to the Field Spell Boot Sector 
Launch's effect, they gain 300 DEF.

00:08:10.740 --> 00:08:12.500
I end my turn.

00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:15.970
Even when he loses all his 
monsters, he hangs in there.

00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:19.990
Go Onizuka is incredible!  
I'm moved to tears!

00:08:19.990 --> 00:08:21.710
Took you long enough.

00:08:22.630 --> 00:08:25.950
This isn't enough to 
break a duelist like him.

00:08:26.290 --> 00:08:27.690
My turn!

00:08:28.430 --> 00:08:29.420
I draw!

00:08:29.420 --> 00:08:33.220
From my hand, I activate the 
spell card, Gouki Re-Match!

00:08:33.550 --> 00:08:38.400
Once per turn, I Special Summon two 
Goukis from my graveyard with different

00:08:38.400 --> 00:08:40.470
Levels in defense position!

00:08:40.470 --> 00:08:44.520
Resurrect, Moonsault and Twistcobra!

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:48.170
Then Moonsault's effect activates!

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:54.410
Once per turn, by returning one Gouki Link 
Monster in my graveyard to my Extra Deck...

00:08:54.410 --> 00:08:59.250
...one Gouki monster in my 
graveyard is added to my hand.

00:08:59.890 --> 00:09:02.770
Appear!  My circuit!

00:09:04.840 --> 00:09:07.760
The summoning conditions are two Goukis!

00:09:07.760 --> 00:09:12.850
I set Moonsault and Twistcobra 
in the Link Markers!

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:16.000
Link Summon!

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:20.480
Appear, Link 2 Gouki Jet Ogre!

00:09:21.380 --> 00:09:26.180
Since Twistcobra was sent to the 
graveyard, its effect activates.

00:09:26.660 --> 00:09:32.490
I add a different Gouki card 
from my deck to my hand!

00:09:32.490 --> 00:09:37.090
Then I summon Gouki Suprex from my hand!

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:41.060
By summoning this monster, 
its effect activates.

00:09:41.060 --> 00:09:45.030
I Special Summon Gouki 
Doubleteam from my hand!

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:49.830
Gouki Jet Ogre's effect!

00:09:49.830 --> 00:09:56.770
Once per turn, by destroying itself, 
all monsters switch to attack position!

00:09:59.500 --> 00:10:04.250
Since Gouki Jet Ogre was sent to the 
graveyard, its effect activates!

00:10:04.250 --> 00:10:10.490
All my Goukis gain 500 ATK 
until the end of the turn!

00:10:10.490 --> 00:10:15.230
From my hand, I activate the 
Equip Spell, Gouki Grit!

00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:20.200
I Special Summon the destroyed Jet 
Ogre and equip it with this card.

00:10:22.170 --> 00:10:24.900
Wow!  He's making a rally!

00:10:26.240 --> 00:10:29.380
Will he attack with his three monsters?

00:10:30.150 --> 00:10:35.620
He'll deal damage, but he can't 
get rid of all of Revolver's LP.

00:10:36.700 --> 00:10:40.040
Even if he destroys the 
Rokkets, they'll resurrect.

00:10:40.040 --> 00:10:42.080
He can destroy his Link Monster...

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:45.120
...but he'll resurrect his 
Rokkets to summon a second one.

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:47.600
What'll he do?

00:10:47.950 --> 00:10:51.330
Appear!  My circuit!

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:55.300
Arrowheads confirmed!

00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:58.340
The summoning conditions 
are at least three Goukis!

00:10:58.340 --> 00:11:05.880
I set Doubleteam, Suprex and Link 
2 Jet Ogre in the Link Markers!

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:09.210
Circuit combine!

00:11:09.780 --> 00:11:11.460
Link Summon!

00:11:11.460 --> 00:11:18.690
Appear, Link 4 Gouki The Giant Ogre!

00:11:23.250 --> 00:11:25.180
How interesting.

00:11:33.970 --> 00:11:36.500
Gouki The Giant Ogre...

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:38.020
It's a new one!

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:40.130
I'm not done.

00:11:40.560 --> 00:11:44.000
My improved Gouki Deck's power 
is only getting started!

00:11:44.000 --> 00:11:47.200
Since Suprex was sent from 
the field to the graveyard...

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:51.560
...I can add a different Gouki 
card from my deck to my hand.

00:11:52.140 --> 00:11:57.930
And when Doubleteam's ATK change 
and is used to Link Summon...

00:11:57.930 --> 00:12:03.370
...Giant Ogre gains 1000 ATK 
until the end of the turn!

00:12:03.370 --> 00:12:11.380
And when Giant Ogre's ATK change, it 
gains 1000 ATK until the end of the turn!

00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:16.280
5000 ATK?

00:12:23.620 --> 00:12:25.610
Hang in there and film!

00:12:25.610 --> 00:12:26.460
Okay!

00:12:26.900 --> 00:12:27.990
Battle!

00:12:27.990 --> 00:12:32.230
Gouki The Giant Ogre attacks Booster Dragon!

00:12:32.740 --> 00:12:36.130
Take this!  Ogre Sword!

00:12:39.910 --> 00:12:42.870
3100 damage instantly?

00:12:42.870 --> 00:12:44.060
He did it!

00:12:44.060 --> 00:12:45.180
He got him!

00:12:45.180 --> 00:12:47.680
Go for it, Onizuka!

00:12:51.820 --> 00:12:54.080
You got me.

00:12:54.460 --> 00:12:56.260
That's payback for earlier.

00:12:56.560 --> 00:13:04.000
Since Booster Dragon was destroyed, I 
Special Summon a Dragon from my graveyard.

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:07.450
Resurrect, Triple Burst Dragon!

00:13:09.020 --> 00:13:11.200
I end my turn.

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:17.510
Giant Ogre and Doubleteam's effects 
end, so their ATK return to normal.

00:13:18.460 --> 00:13:20.580
I always improve.

00:13:20.580 --> 00:13:23.150
That's what makes me Go Onizuka!

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:25.620
My turn!  I draw!

00:13:25.620 --> 00:13:32.960
I tribute Triple Burst Dragon to Special 
Summon Booster Dragon from my graveyard.

00:13:35.200 --> 00:13:42.600
And due to Triple Burst's effect, I Special 
Summon a Level 4 or lower Dragon from my hand!

00:13:42.940 --> 00:13:45.500
Appear, Hibernation Dragon!

00:13:46.780 --> 00:13:49.770
When Hibernation Dragon 
is Special Summoned...

00:13:49.770 --> 00:13:56.910
...I can add a Level 4 or lower Dark Dragon 
from my graveyard to my hand and summon it.

00:13:56.910 --> 00:13:59.000
Appear, Magnarokket Dragon!

00:14:00.960 --> 00:14:09.550
Due to the Field Spell Boot Sector Launch's 
effect, Magnarokket Dragon gains 300 ATK!

00:14:09.550 --> 00:14:15.170
And due to Booster Dragon's effect, 
Magnarokket gains 500 ATK!

00:14:15.170 --> 00:14:20.380
But Magnarokket's effect now 
activates and self-destructs!

00:14:24.990 --> 00:14:29.190
Then I choose one monster on the 
field and send it to the graveyard.

00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:34.150
I choose Gouki The Giant Ogre!

00:14:38.800 --> 00:14:43.320
If Giant Ogre is destroyed, Go 
Onizuka's field will be empty.

00:14:43.320 --> 00:14:46.830
If he's attacked directly, 
it's the end of the story!

00:14:47.140 --> 00:14:48.300
Fire!

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:52.840
Giant Ogre's effect!

00:14:52.840 --> 00:14:56.540
It's not affected by monsters 
with equal or fewer ATK!

00:15:02.680 --> 00:15:04.080
Onizuka!

00:15:05.260 --> 00:15:06.890
Too bad!

00:15:07.370 --> 00:15:09.980
You're so stubborn.

00:15:09.980 --> 00:15:14.550
Until now, I've battled 
in front of large crowds.

00:15:17.200 --> 00:15:25.320
To entertain the many children who root for 
me, I tried to make duels more exciting.

00:15:26.620 --> 00:15:28.920
But I realized I'm all alone.

00:15:28.920 --> 00:15:31.920
There are no fans rooting for me here.

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:36.110
I realized...

00:15:36.480 --> 00:15:38.510
We always duel alone.

00:15:38.510 --> 00:15:42.320
We fight for ourselves, not for anyone else!

00:15:42.320 --> 00:15:45.930
That's why I decided to fight for myself!

00:15:46.530 --> 00:15:49.780
To prove that I'm the strongest!

00:15:49.780 --> 00:15:54.230
For my thirst for victory 
that's deep in my heart!

00:15:54.840 --> 00:15:57.920
So bring it on with all your strength!

00:16:00.160 --> 00:16:03.910
Fine.  As you wish.

00:16:06.840 --> 00:16:09.880
What is Revolver going to do?

00:16:12.090 --> 00:16:15.350
With that last attack, 
their LP are about equal.

00:16:15.780 --> 00:16:17.560
He has zero cards in his hand.

00:16:17.560 --> 00:16:19.630
But look at his field.

00:16:22.100 --> 00:16:24.900
He will summon a Link 4.

00:16:24.900 --> 00:16:26.600
Borreload Dragon!

00:16:26.600 --> 00:16:31.100
Manifest!  The future circuit 
that lights up my path!

00:16:32.370 --> 00:16:34.020
Arrowheads confirmed!

00:16:34.020 --> 00:16:37.260
The summoning conditions are 
at least three Effect Monsters!

00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:44.460
I set Hibernation, Shelrokket and Link 
2 Booster Dragon in the Link Markers!

00:16:45.620 --> 00:16:47.590
Circuit combine!

00:16:47.590 --> 00:16:51.320
My gale that slices open the closed world!

00:16:51.740 --> 00:16:52.820
Link Summon!

00:16:52.820 --> 00:16:57.800
Appear, Link 4 Borrelsword Dragon!

00:16:59.180 --> 00:17:00.640
That looks tough!

00:17:01.380 --> 00:17:06.370
It has the same ATK as Borreload, but does 
it have a different effect for this situation?

00:17:06.370 --> 00:17:08.340
Onizuka is in trouble again?

00:17:08.990 --> 00:17:13.860
I can't believe you forced me 
to play Borrelsword Dragon.

00:17:13.860 --> 00:17:16.700
But it's the end of the line.

00:17:16.700 --> 00:17:23.550
I don't agree with the lame 
idea of fighting for others.

00:17:23.550 --> 00:17:25.970
Or for myself.

00:17:25.970 --> 00:17:29.560
I just carry out my goal.  That's all!

00:17:29.960 --> 00:17:31.030
Battle!

00:17:31.030 --> 00:17:35.510
Borrelsword Dragon attacks Giant Ogre!

00:17:38.980 --> 00:17:40.920
Ogre Sword!

00:17:55.460 --> 00:17:57.990
What?  It's the most important part!

00:17:59.930 --> 00:18:02.190
Why can't we see it?

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:04.530
Go...

00:18:07.210 --> 00:18:12.740
Borrelsword Dragon can't be 
destroyed in battle once per turn!

00:18:12.740 --> 00:18:16.450
Giant Ogre also isn't destroyed in battle!

00:18:16.450 --> 00:18:19.980
Nor affected by monsters 
with equal or fewer ATK!

00:18:19.980 --> 00:18:22.450
In that case, Borrelsword's effect!

00:18:22.930 --> 00:18:29.920
By battling Giant Ogre, it gains half 
its ATK until the end of the turn!

00:18:29.920 --> 00:18:33.140
It now has more ATK than Giant Ogre!

00:18:33.140 --> 00:18:35.390
Effects can affect it now!

00:18:35.390 --> 00:18:39.660
Then Giant Ogre's ATK are halved!

00:18:43.600 --> 00:18:45.830
1500 ATK!

00:18:45.830 --> 00:18:49.540
Metalrokket has 2000 ATK, 
so it'll affect it too!

00:18:49.540 --> 00:18:52.510
Borrelsword Dragon's additional effect!

00:18:52.510 --> 00:18:55.520
It switches Metalrokket 
Dragon to defense position.

00:18:55.520 --> 00:19:00.670
But Metalrokket's effect now 
activates and self-destructs!

00:19:05.920 --> 00:19:12.230
All your cards in the Zones vertical 
to Metalrokket are destroyed!

00:19:15.210 --> 00:19:17.740
Zero Bullet Fire!

00:19:21.870 --> 00:19:24.100
No!  Onizuka!

00:19:29.420 --> 00:19:31.940
He survived!  How?

00:19:34.860 --> 00:19:42.020
When Giant Ogre's ATK change, it gains 
1000 ATK until the end of the turn.

00:19:42.770 --> 00:19:45.720
That effect was already active!

00:19:46.840 --> 00:19:53.550
Since Giant Ogre's ATK were greater than 
Metalrokket's again, your effect was negated.

00:19:53.900 --> 00:19:55.780
Too bad!

00:19:56.080 --> 00:20:01.010
I don't feel like winning so inelegantly.

00:20:02.700 --> 00:20:09.440
When I use Zero Bullet Fire during my 
turn, Borrelsword can attack again.

00:20:09.440 --> 00:20:10.230
What?

00:20:10.530 --> 00:20:12.460
This is the end.

00:20:13.140 --> 00:20:16.530
Electric Borrelsword Slash!

00:20:47.550 --> 00:20:48.940
Onizuka...

00:20:51.420 --> 00:20:54.400
Onizuka won, right?

00:20:54.400 --> 00:20:55.950
Yes, of course.

00:20:55.950 --> 00:20:59.150
That's right!  Go Onizuka never loses!

00:21:00.630 --> 00:21:03.610
Isn't that right, Go?

00:21:06.340 --> 00:21:08.530
He survived again!

00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:09.320
No.

00:21:11.300 --> 00:21:15.320
Go Onizuka has 0 LP.

00:21:21.940 --> 00:21:26.160
Playmaker!  This was the best I could do.

00:21:26.160 --> 00:21:31.640
Go Onizuka!  Thanks to you, I was 
able to learn his strategies.

00:21:33.350 --> 00:21:34.880
I leave the rest to you.

00:21:39.560 --> 00:21:41.190
Playmaker.

00:21:41.810 --> 00:21:46.050
We're the only two duelists 
left in this world.

00:21:46.050 --> 00:21:49.520
It's finally time to bring this to an end.

00:21:51.150 --> 00:21:52.520
Yeah.

00:22:08.850 --> 00:22:15.690
My life is like detestably bad graffiti

00:22:16.050 --> 00:22:22.830
But when you looked at 
me, I felt I wasn't alone

00:22:23.230 --> 00:22:30.030
I'm glad that I'm alive  I truly am

00:22:30.530 --> 00:22:37.410
What I couldn't say before, I can say now

00:22:38.240 --> 00:22:44.630
Within the sadness that I kept holding down

00:22:45.020 --> 00:22:48.880
There were fragments of power

00:22:48.880 --> 00:22:55.990
No one can take away my light to the future

00:22:55.990 --> 00:23:03.430
The chronicles of life only has a few lines

00:23:03.430 --> 00:23:10.500
People I meet, my regrets – they're 
all like ultramarine diamonds to me

00:23:10.500 --> 00:23:17.840
You've always confront loneliness by yourself

00:23:17.840 --> 00:23:24.590
I bet we can now laugh 
together, forever and ever
